1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:02,080
An empty corridor.

2
00:00:02,480 --> 00:00:04,360
Or the start of a mystery?

3
00:00:04,740 --> 00:00:05,820
Meet Yuvo.

4
00:00:07,400 --> 00:00:12,360
Start with an idea: a woman can talk to abandoned buildings.

5
00:00:12,800 --> 00:00:14,770
Their memories are incomplete.

6
00:00:15,400 --> 00:00:17,390
Gemini plans the research.

7
00:00:17,780 --> 00:00:20,460
Parallel searches nearby stories and audience reactions,

8
00:00:20,480 --> 00:00:22,740
so you’re building on evidence.

9
00:00:27,400 --> 00:00:29,550
Eleven sources. One useful direction:

10
00:00:29,890 --> 00:00:34,240
let the building’s damage shape what it remembers.

11
00:00:35,400 --> 00:00:38,160
Now, agentic video understanding.

12
00:00:38,640 --> 00:00:40,000
Attach a real cut.

13
00:00:40,560 --> 00:00:43,360
Gemini checks the frames against your premise.

14
00:00:43,760 --> 00:00:45,880
It sees the abandoned setting,

15
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:48,000
but catches the missing protagonist.

16
00:00:48,480 --> 00:00:49,560
Click a timestamp.

17
00:00:49,880 --> 00:00:51,080
See exactly what it means.

18
00:00:53,950 --> 00:00:56,110
Let’s iterate. We add a deadline

19
00:00:56,110 --> 00:00:58,990
and two conflicting memories to the same footage.

20
00:00:59,380 --> 00:01:00,790
Upload the new cut.

21
00:01:01,640 --> 00:01:04,490
Gemini compares both videos.

22
00:01:04,770 --> 00:01:06,530
It spots the new text,

23
00:01:06,530 --> 00:01:08,890
and tells us what still needs work:

24
00:01:09,100 --> 00:01:11,960
show the woman interacting with the building.

25
00:01:12,200 --> 00:01:14,620
That’s a specific shot we can make next.

26
00:01:16,200 --> 00:01:19,530
Powered by Gemini, Parallel, and Google Cloud Run.

27
00:01:19,960 --> 00:01:23,170
Yuvo. Big idea. Better story.
